# CSAD Lab - Ansible Automation

Automation for two fleets of lab VMs on vSphere/vCenter, configuring dual-NIC
networking, unique hostnames, time sync, and log shipping to a central
VictoriaLogs instance. The end goal is **automatically labeled, time-synced
logs** (and packet captures) that can be correlated across all machines.

## Fleets

| Fleet | OS | Count | Notes |
|-------|----|-------|-------|
| **vulhub** | Ubuntu Server 24.04 | 14 | Modern stack: netplan, systemd, Promtail |
| **metasploitable2** | Ubuntu 8.04 (Hardy) | 7 | Ancient: Python 2.5, SysVinit, 32-bit — all playbooks are `raw`-only |

Both fleets are **dual-homed**:
- **Management NIC** — the `192.168.77.x` address Ansible connects over. Holds
  NO default route; only specific routes to internal lab subnets via
  `192.168.77.1`.
- **Internet NIC** — DHCP on the `10.10.x` VLAN; owns the default route.

Internal subnets routed via the management gateway (`192.168.77.1`):
- `192.168.77.0/24` — management subnet
- `192.168.71.0/24` — VPN / control-path (WSL control node reaches the VMs
  through here)
- `192.168.85.0/24` — VictoriaLogs server (`192.168.85.125:9428`)

## Directory layout

```
csad-ansible/
├── ansible.cfg
├── inventory.ini                    # [vulhub] and [metasploitable2] groups
├── README.md                        # this file
│
├── vulhub/                          # Ubuntu 24.04
│   ├── configure-netplan.yml        # dual-NIC routing (auto-detects interfaces)
│   ├── set-hostnames.yml            # unique hostnames from inventory names
│   ├── vmware-logs.yml              # Promtail log shipping + NTP (timesyncd)
│   ├── templates/netplan-dual-nic.yaml.j2
│   ├── promtail/{config.yaml.j2,promtail.service.j2}
│   └── files/promtail-linux-amd64{,.zip}
│
└── metasploitable2/                 # Ubuntu 8.04 (raw-only)
    ├── configure-network.yml        # dual-NIC routing (/etc/network/interfaces)
    ├── set-hostnames.yml            # unique hostnames
    ├── configure-ntp.yml            # ntpdate -u on a 1-minute cron
    ├── ship-logs.yml                # curl-based VictoriaLogs shipper
    ├── templates/interfaces.j2      # reference only (embedded in playbook)
    └── files/{vlogs-shipper.sh,vlogs-shipper-init.sh}
```

Paths inside playbooks are relative to the playbook, so `templates/` and
`files/` must sit next to their playbook. Run everything from the project root
with the folder prefix (e.g. `ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini vulhub/...`).

