## Prerequisites

### vSphere (manual — cannot be done by these playbooks)

Add a SECOND network adapter to every VM, on the internet VLAN port group,
"connect at power on":
- **vulhub:** adapter type **VMXNET3**.
- **metasploitable2:** adapter type **E1000** — the 8.04 kernel has no vmxnet3
  driver, so a vmxnet3 NIC never appears. After adding, power the VM OFF then
  ON (8.04 does not hotplug PCI NICs).

VictoriaLogs must be running and reachable at `192.168.85.125:9428` (HTTP
ingestion + UI). No syslog listener is required — both fleets ship over HTTP.

### Control node (WSL)

```bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y ansible sshpass
```

Keep the project in the WSL Linux filesystem (e.g. `~/csad-ansible`), NOT under
`/mnt/c/...` — Windows-mounted dirs show as world-writable (777) and Ansible
refuses to load `ansible.cfg` from them.

```bash
cd ~/csad-ansible && chmod 755 ~/csad-ansible
```

### inventory.ini

Two groups. The metasploitable2 group needs legacy-SSH args (modern OpenSSH
rejects its old key algorithms):

```ini
[vulhub]
vulhub-1-1 ansible_host=192.168.77.235
# ... 14 hosts ...

[vulhub:vars]
ansible_user=vulhub-ubuntu-server
ansible_password=vulhub
ansible_become_pass=vulhub

[metasploitable2]
metas2-1 ansible_host=192.168.77.249
# ... 7 hosts ...

[metasploitable2:vars]
ansible_user=msfadmin
ansible_password=msfadmin
ansible_become_pass=msfadmin
ansible_ssh_common_args=-oHostKeyAlgorithms=+ssh-rsa,ssh-dss -oPubkeyAcceptedKeyTypes=+ssh-rsa
```

### ansible.cfg

```ini
[defaults]
inventory = inventory.ini
host_key_checking = False
```

