## Run order

Within each fleet the order matters: **network → hostnames → NTP → logs**.
Network first (everything needs internet + the route to VictoriaLogs);
hostnames before logs (so logs are labeled); NTP independent but before relying
on timestamps. The two fleets are independent of each other.

Test each step on one host (`--limit`) before the whole fleet.

### 0. Connectivity check

```bash
cd ~/csad-ansible
ansible -i inventory.ini vulhub -m ping
ansible -i inventory.ini metasploitable2 -m raw -a "hostname"
```

### vulhub (Ubuntu 24.04)

```bash
# 1. Network
ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini vulhub/configure-netplan.yml --limit vulhub-1-1
ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini vulhub/configure-netplan.yml

# 2. Hostnames
ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini vulhub/set-hostnames.yml

# 3. Promtail + NTP
ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini vulhub/vmware-logs.yml --limit vulhub-1-1
ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini vulhub/vmware-logs.yml
```

### metasploitable2 (Ubuntu 8.04) — keep a vCenter console open for step 1

```bash
# 1. Network  (no auto-revert on this OS — console open as a safety net)
ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini metasploitable2/configure-network.yml --limit metas2-1
ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini metasploitable2/configure-network.yml

# 2. Hostnames
ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini metasploitable2/set-hostnames.yml

# 3. NTP  (repoints apt to old-releases, installs, schedules ntpdate cron)
ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini metasploitable2/configure-ntp.yml --limit metas2-1
ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini metasploitable2/configure-ntp.yml

# 4. Log shipping  (curl shipper -> VictoriaLogs 9428)
ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini metasploitable2/ship-logs.yml --limit metas2-1
ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini metasploitable2/ship-logs.yml
```

