## Verification

### vulhub

```bash
ansible -i inventory.ini vulhub -m command -a "ip route get 8.8.8.8" --become
ansible -i inventory.ini vulhub -m command -a "timedatectl show -p NTPSynchronized" --become
ansible -i inventory.ini vulhub -m command -a "systemctl is-active promtail" --become
```

### metasploitable2

```bash
# routing (internet should exit via eth1)
ansible -i inventory.ini metasploitable2 -m raw -a "ip route get 8.8.8.8" --become
# VictoriaLogs reachable over HTTP
ansible -i inventory.ini metasploitable2 -m raw -a "curl -sS --max-time 5 -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' http://192.168.85.125:9428/" --become
# ntpdate cron firing (wait ~2 min after the NTP step)
ansible -i inventory.ini metasploitable2 -m raw -a "grep ntpdate /var/log/syslog | tail -1" --become
# shipper running on all 7
ansible -i inventory.ini metasploitable2 -m raw -a "pgrep -f vlogs-shipper >/dev/null && echo shipping || echo DOWN" --become
```

### End-to-end

In the VictoriaLogs UI, open the `hostname` field values — all 21 machines
(`vulhub-*` and `metas2-*`) should appear as log sources.

